{"book":16,"chapter":11,"rubric":"FROM ASSEMBLER TO C / PROJECTS AND TOOLING / CHAPTER 11","slides":[{"title":"What is UB","sub":"Chapter 11 · no guarantees","short":"UB","main":"Undefined behavior: total freedom for the compiler.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Three kinds","Compiler freedom","Not \"something odd\""],"captions":["Implementation-defined (documented), unspecified (several valid outcomes), and undefined behavior: the standard promises nothing","With UB a program may work, crash, return garbage or behave differently in another compiler version","Not a \"strange result\" but no guarantees: the compiler need not check such cases and will not"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"implementation-defined","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":76.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"unspecified","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":90.0,"y":112.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"undefined (UB)","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":290.0,"y":76.0,"text":"best\nto worst","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"works","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"crashes","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":70.0,"y":90.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"garbage","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":190.0,"y":90.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"otherwise tomorrow","tone":"muted","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"anything goes","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int a[4];","a[4] = 1;   // ✕ UB — who knows what happens"],"bad":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[14.1,34.8]}]},{"title":"Main groups","sub":"Memory, arithmetic, other","short":"Groups","main":"Bounds, pointers, signed arithmetic, aliasing.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Memory","Arithmetic","Other"],"captions":["Out of bounds, NULL and dangling dereference, read after free, double free, returning a local address","Signed integer overflow, division by zero, shift by type width or more, reading an uninitialized variable","Strict aliasing and alignment, writing to a string literal, overlapping memcpy, thread data races"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["a[n] = 0;          // out of bounds","*p;               // p == NULL","free(p); *p;       // after free","return &local;    // no frame"],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["INT_MAX + 1;       // UB","x / 0;             // UB","1u << 32;          // UB","int v; v + 1;       // UB"],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["*(int *)&f;        // aliasing","char *s = \"ab\"; s[0] = 'x';","memcpy(b + 2, b, 6);   // overlap","// thread race"],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[15.5,27.2]}]},{"title":"Optimizer and UB","sub":"Reasoning by contradiction","short":"Optimizer","main":"Checks vanish; the bug shows only in -O2.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["x + 1 > x","Check after dereference","Read the assembly"],"captions":["For signed x the compiler turns x + 1 > x into true: overflow \"cannot happen\"","if (!p) after *p is removed as redundant: once dereferenced, p is not NULL","gcc -O2 -S shows what is left: checks and branches vanish, and the bug shows only in the optimized build"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["int f(int x) { return x + 1 > x; }",""],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"code","id":"a","x":130.0,"y":100.0,"lines":["li a0, 1","ret"],"lang":"asm","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":110.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":270.0,"y":106.0,"text":"always 1","tone":"yellow","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["int v = p->a;       // dereferenced","if (!p) return -1;  // removed!","return v;"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["$ gcc -O2 -S main.c","$ gcc -O0 -S main.c"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[18.6,30.9]}]},{"title":"Uninitialized data","sub":"Stack leftovers","short":"Uninit.","main":"Initialize at declaration; calloc gives zeros.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Stack leftovers","malloc does not zero","How to defend"],"captions":["A local variable gets whatever earlier calls left on the stack; you must not read it","malloc returns memory as is; calloc gives zeros; a program works for years while a zero happens to lie there","Initialize at declaration; -Wall -Wextra catch some cases; for the rest — MSan and Valgrind"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":50.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"frame f: old data","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":86.0,"w":140.0,"h":26.0,"text":"frame g: int s;","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":160.0,"y1":62.0,"x2":160.0,"y2":74.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":280.0,"y":86.0,"text":"s = garbage\nfrom f","tone":"red","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int *a = malloc(n * sizeof *a);   // not zeros","int *b = calloc(n, sizeof *b);   // zeros"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int s = 0;","int a[8] = {0};","-Wall -Wextra -Wmaybe-uninitialized"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[12.9,23.9]}]},{"title":"Lifetime","sub":"Dangling pointers","short":"Lifetime","main":"Returning a local, use-after-free, leaving a block.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Returning a local","After free","Outside a block"],"captions":["A function returned the address of its local variable: the frame is gone, the pointer points nowhere","free released the block but the pointer stayed: memory may keep old data for years","A pointer to a variable of a block that has ended: the same thing on the stack"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["int *f(void) {","    int x = 5;","    return &x;   // ✕","}"],"bad":[2],"lang":"c","size":11.0,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["free(p);","*p = 1;        // ✕ use-after-free","p = NULL;      // guard"],"bad":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["int *p;","{ int x = 5; p = &x; }","*p;   // ✕ stack-use-after-scope"],"bad":[2],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[12.2,23.9]}]},{"title":"Warnings and analysis","sub":"-Wall -Wextra -Werror","short":"Warnings","main":"Static analyzers find bugs on paths never run.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Warnings","-Werror","Static analysis"],"captions":["-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic, and also -Wshadow, -Wconversion, -Wformat=2: shadowing, precision loss, wrong formats","-Werror turns warnings into errors: in a clean build every new warning is noticed at once","-fanalyzer in gcc, clang-tidy and cppcheck find bugs on paths the tests never reach"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["gcc -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic \\","    -Wshadow -Wconversion -Wformat=2 main.c"],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["CFLAGS = -Wall -Wextra -Werror","main.c:7: error: unused variable 'x'"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["gcc -fanalyzer main.c","clang-tidy main.c --","cppcheck --enable=all src/"],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[15.4,23.7]}]},{"title":"AddressSanitizer","sub":"Red zones","short":"ASan","main":"Bounds, use-after-free, double free and leaks with a report.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Red zones","What it finds","Report"],"captions":["ASan surrounds blocks with forbidden zones and keeps a shadow map: is each byte accessible or not","Out of bounds on heap, stack and globals, use-after-free, double free, leaks; about a twofold slowdown","-fsanitize=address -g -fno-omit-frame-pointer gives a report with a call stack and where memory was allocated and freed"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"z0","x":70.0,"y":66.0,"w":96.0,"h":34.0,"text":"red","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"z1","x":170.0,"y":66.0,"w":96.0,"h":34.0,"text":"data","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"z2","x":270.0,"y":66.0,"w":96.0,"h":34.0,"text":"red","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":124.0,"text":"red zone access → report and stop","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"heap-buffer-overflow","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"stack-buffer-overflow","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"heap-use-after-free","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":90.0,"y":130.0,"w":130.0,"h":24.0,"text":"detected memory leaks","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":290.0,"y":86.0,"text":"×2 time","size":9.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":10.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow","WRITE of size 4 at 0x… thread T0","    #0 fill main.c:12","    #1 main main.c:30","allocated by thread T0 here:  #1 main main.c:28"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":8.0,"lh":20.0,"w":350.0}]],"cues":[8.6,23.4]}]},{"title":"UBSan, MSan, TSan","sub":"Separate builds","short":"UBSan","main":"-fsanitize=undefined and -fno-sanitize-recover=all.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["UBSan","Do not continue","MSan and TSan"],"captions":["-fsanitize=undefined inserts checks: signed overflow, shifts, division by zero, NULL, alignment, array bounds, VLA","By default it prints and continues; -fno-sanitize-recover=all stops the program at the first error","MSan (clang) — uninitialized reads, TSan — data races; sanitizers barely combine, so make separate builds"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["runtime error: signed integer overflow","runtime error: shift exponent 32 …","runtime error: division by zero","runtime error: index 8 out of bounds"],"bad":[0,1,2,3],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["gcc -fsanitize=undefined \\","    -fno-sanitize-recover=all main.c"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":80.0,"y":50.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"ASan + UBSan","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":80.0,"y":100.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"MSan","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":250.0,"y":50.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"TSan","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":250.0,"y":105.0,"text":"separate\nbuilds","size":9.5}]],"cues":[20.8,30.7]}]},{"title":"gdb","sub":"Breakpoints and the stack","short":"gdb","main":"-g -O0; break, next, print, backtrace, watch.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Build and run","Steps and values","Stack and memory"],"captions":["For gdb build with -g -O0: otherwise variables vanish from the code; break sets a breakpoint, run starts","next — a line without entering, step — entering, print — a value, watch — follow a variable, finish — leave the function","backtrace shows the call stack, x/8xw — memory in hex; a core dump lets you analyze a crash after the fact"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["$ gcc -g -O0 main.c -o app","$ gdb ./app","(gdb) break main","(gdb) run"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["(gdb) next","(gdb) print n","$1 = 7","(gdb) watch total","(gdb) finish"],"hl":[1,3],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":20.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["(gdb) backtrace","#0 sum (a=0x…, n=3) at main.c:8","#1 main () at main.c:20","(gdb) x/4xw a"],"hl":[0,3],"lang":"c","size":9.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[10.9,31.7]}]},{"title":"assert and tests","sub":"Invariants and regressions","short":"assert","main":"Turn every bug found into a test.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["assert","static_assert","Test from a bug"],"captions":["assert(cond) checks an invariant and on failure prints the condition, file and line; -DNDEBUG turns it off — no side effects inside","_Static_assert checks a condition at compile time: type sizes, constants","Tracing to stderr with a call-site macro is often faster than a debugger; a found bug becomes a regression test"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["#include <assert.h>","assert(i < n);","// Assertion `i < n' failed. main.c:12"],"hl":[1],"lang":"c","size":10.0,"lh":26.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["_Static_assert(sizeof(int) == 4,","                \"32-bit int required\");"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["#define TRACE(...) fprintf(stderr, __VA_ARGS__)","void test_bug_123(void) {","    assert(parse(\"1e\") == -1);","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":22.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[21.1,26.1]}]},{"title":"Valgrind","sub":"No rebuild","short":"Valgrind","main":"A fallback; slow but exact.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["No rebuild","What it finds","When needed"],"captions":["Valgrind runs a ready binary on a virtual processor and monitors every memory access","Memcheck finds uninitialized reads, leaks and heap overflows; tens of times slower","A fallback when sources are hard to rebuild, and a source of exact leak reports; usually ASan first"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["$ valgrind ./app","==1234== Memcheck, a memory error detector"],"hl":[0],"lang":"c","size":10.5,"lh":28.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["Invalid read of size 4","Conditional jump depends on uninitialised value","100 bytes in 1 blocks are definitely lost"],"bad":[0,1,2],"lang":"c","size":9.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"ASan + UBSan","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":250.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Valgrind","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"fast — first; fallback — later","size":9.5}]],"cues":[13.4,28.3]}]},{"title":"A bug-hunting method","sub":"Shrinking, bisection, fuzzing","short":"Method","main":"Reproduce, shrink, test a hypothesis.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Reproduce and shrink","Bisection","Fuzzing"],"captions":["Reproduce reliably, then shrink the input while the bug remains","If the bug appeared between versions, binary search through history finds the guilty commit in log₂ n steps","A fuzzer feeds mutated data under sanitizers and catches crashes; every find becomes a regression test"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":60.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"1000 bytes","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"40 bytes","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":300.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"7 bytes","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":100.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":140.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":220.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":260.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":126.0,"text":"bug remains","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"v1","x":28.0,"y":76.0,"w":40.0,"h":28.0,"text":"v1","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v2","x":74.0,"y":76.0,"w":40.0,"h":28.0,"text":"v2","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v3","x":120.0,"y":76.0,"w":40.0,"h":28.0,"text":"v3","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v4","x":166.0,"y":76.0,"w":40.0,"h":28.0,"text":"v4","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v5","x":212.0,"y":76.0,"w":40.0,"h":28.0,"text":"v5","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v6","x":258.0,"y":76.0,"w":40.0,"h":28.0,"text":"v6","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v7","x":304.0,"y":76.0,"w":40.0,"h":28.0,"text":"v7","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"v8","x":350.0,"y":76.0,"w":40.0,"h":28.0,"text":"v8","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"first bad — in 3 checks","size":9.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"generator","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":76.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"program + ASan","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":310.0,"y":76.0,"w":80.0,"h":30.0,"text":"crash → test","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":120.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":140.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":250.0,"y1":76.0,"x2":270.0,"y2":76.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[12.3,26.1]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What next","short":"Summary","main":"Next — hash tables, trees and heaps.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["UB","Layers of defense","Next"],"captions":["UB — no guarantees; the optimizer exploits it; main groups: bounds, pointers, signed arithmetic, uninitialized data","Warnings and analysis at compile time, ASan and UBSan in tests, debugger and assert when hunting, Valgrind as fallback; every bug into a test","Next — hash tables, trees and heaps in C"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"bounds","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":220.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"pointers","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"sign and shifts","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":220.0,"y":100.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"uninit.","tone":"red","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":50.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"-Wall -Werror","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":50.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"ASan + UBSan","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":130.0,"y":96.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"gdb, assert","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":250.0,"y":96.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"valgrind","tone":"muted","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"text","id":"a~text","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"text":"hash tables · trees · heaps","tone":"green","size":11.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"b~text","x":180.0,"y":104.0,"text":"next chapter","size":10.0}]],"cues":[10.1,18.7]}]}]}